========================================================================
  ERROR DIFFUSION: RANDOM WALK AS CHANNEL (n=5)
========================================================================


  The meta-graph IS a communication channel:
  - Sender encodes tournament class C (codeword)
  - Channel flips t random arcs (t-step random walk)
  - Receiver observes class C' (possibly different)

  After t steps: Pr[C' = D | start = C] = P^t[C, D]

  The CHANNEL CAPACITY depends on the mixing time:
  - t << t_mix: transmitted class is close to original (low noise)
  - t >> t_mix: transmitted class is random (maximum noise)

  The spectral gap determines the crossover:
  - gap = 0.4803 → t_mix ≈ 5
  - So t ≈ 5 steps is the noise floor

  CHANNEL TRANSITION AFTER t STEPS:
    t= 1: avg Pr[stay] = 0.0000, max Pr[error to single class] = 0.5000
    t= 2: avg Pr[stay] = 0.2346, max Pr[error to single class] = 0.2444
    t= 5: avg Pr[stay] = 0.0811, max Pr[error to single class] = 0.1997
    t=10: avg Pr[stay] = 0.1044, max Pr[error to single class] = 0.1735
    t=20: avg Pr[stay] = 0.1002, max Pr[error to single class] = 0.1670

